  "_notation": {
    "_comment": "A session pattern is a LIST of sessions. Order does not matter - what matters is how many sessions there are and how long each is. This sidesteps the right-to-left ambiguity of the printed tables entirely.",
    "whole": "n hours, whole class together",
    "group": "n hours, class split into groups. Each group attends n hours, so the TEACHER works n x (number of groups). This is why pupil hours and teacher hours differ.",
    "fortnight_whole": "n hours, whole class, every SECOND week (Week A / Week B)",
    "fortnight_group": "every second week, in groups. circled(2) = 1h per group ON THE SAME DAY. circled(4) = 2h per group.",
    "alt_whole_1_2": "alternates weekly: 1 hour one week, 2 hours the next, whole class",
    "alt_whole1_group4": "alternates weekly: week A = 1h whole class, week B = 4h in groups (2h per group). The two MUST sit in non-simultaneous slots across weeks A and B.",
    "pilot_only": "weekly group session that applies ONLY to pilot institutes (المعاهد النموذجية). See open question Q1.",
    "alt_mech_elec": "two group sessions alternating between mechanical engineering (الهندسة الآلية) and electrical engineering (الهندسة الكهربائية)"
  },

  "_groups_assumption": {
    "value": 2,
    "warning": "Teacher hours below assume a class splits into TWO groups. The sport-stream table confirms it: Biology = 1h whole + 2h group -> pupil 3, teacher 5 (= 1 + 2x2). If this school ever uses three groups, every teacher_hours figure changes. See open question Q5.",
    "conflict": "Majd said a '3 hour' session at this school is really 1.5h per group because the lab is small. The ministry notation means the OPPOSITE: (3) = 3 hours FOR EACH group. Unresolved - see Q22."
  },

